@@ -54,7 +54,8 @@ http://nodejs.org/api/events.html
 ### Contextual emits
 
 We've upgraded the API of the `EventEmitter.on`, `EventEmitter.once` and
-`EventEmitter.removeListener` to accept an extra argument which is the `context`
+`EventEmitter.removeListener` and `EventEmitter.removeListenersByContext` to
+accept an extra argument which is the `context`
 or `this` value that should be set for the emitted events. This means you no
 longer have the overhead of an event that required `fn.bind` in order to get a
 custom `this` value.
@@ -70,8 +71,15 @@ function emitted() {
 EE.once('event-name', emitted, context);
 EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
+EE.removeListenersByContext(context); // returns the number of registrations removed
 ```
 
+`removeListenersByContext` removes every registration across all event names
+whose stored context is strictly equal to the supplied value. Duplicate and
+one-time registrations are counted separately. As with `on` and `once`, an
+omitted or falsy context is normalized to the emitter itself, so those
+listeners can be removed with `EE.removeListenersByContext(EE)`.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
